  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Acetal is form from the reaction of aldehyde with excess of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9c894103-33d1-4e7d-97e5-851a80a590e4-image29.png\" /></p><p>Formation of an acetal occurs when the hydroxyl group of a hemiacetal becomes protonated and is lost as water. The carbocation that is produced is then rapidly attacked by a molecule of alcohol. Loss of the proton from the attached alcohol gives the acetal.</p>",
